0134 — DFlash/DSpark drafters must not get eagle KV-cache block handling (rc1-native port of the idea in vllm-project/vllm
PR #54163 by Ledgero, which targets a newer main with #53388's use_eagle_block_drop; rc1 lacks that helper, so this
carries the predicate to every rc1 site that keys KV handling on use_eagle(): the scheduler's KVCacheManager(use_eagle=…)
and Mamba back-off, the offloading connector's draft-group fallback, and kv_cache_utils' eagle-group annotation/warning).
Mechanism on rc1 + Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2 (R165 cell A): no KV group is annotated as the draft's, so every group is
treated as a draft group; rc1's MambaManager now honours drop_eagle_block and needs two consecutive chunks that align-mode
checkpointing never produces -> prefix-cache hits 0 on identical re-sends (v0.28.0 same shape: 51,584 hits, TTFT 0.45 s).
Tree-root relative (-p1 from site-packages). Verified: verify.sh (apply + py_compile); metal: r165b warm revisit.

diff --color -u -r a/vllm/config/speculative.py b/vllm/config/speculative.py
--- a/vllm/config/speculative.py	2026-09-03 12:43:19
+++ b/vllm/config/speculative.py	2026-09-03 12:43:19
@@ -1846,6 +1846,15 @@
         # TODO(ben): Refactor this so the naming is clearer
         return self.method in ("eagle", "eagle3", "mtp", "dflash", "dspark")
 
+    def use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache(self) -> bool:
+        # Only eagle-family drafters share (and pollute via their lookahead KV
+        # write) the target's full-attention KV cache groups. DFlash/DSpark draft
+        # from their own KV cache and never write target blocks, so the KV cache
+        # manager must not apply eagle block handling to them (vllm-project/vllm
+        # #53477, #54163): on a hybrid model in align mode it turns prefix-cache
+        # reuse off entirely.
+        return self.method in ("eagle", "eagle3", "mtp")
+
     def use_dflash(self) -> bool:
         return self.method == "dflash"
 
